## Always

1. `search` or `list_tasks` before creating — no duplicates.
2. New work: `create_task` with detailed description (goal, requirement IDs, decisions, files, out-of-scope), `priority` (`urgent|high|medium|low|no-priority`), `status`, `userId`.
3. Labels: `list_workspace_labels`, match **name**, `attach_label_to_task`. Required: Phase 1–4 or v2; area (Desktop/Backend/Tax-Engine/Auth/Infra/UI/PDF/Offline/Audit/Product); type (Feature/Bug/Chore/Docs/Spike/UAT/Epic/Blocker); requirement (ENT-01…); triage (`ready-for-agent` | `ready-for-human` | `needs-info` | `needs-triage`); `Agent` or `Human`.
4. Assignee: Agent work → Cursor Grok userId (else Clemens + `Agent`). Human UAT/decisions → Clemens + `Human` + `ready-for-human`.
5. Keep in sync: start work → `in-progress`; wait on human → `in-review`; shipped → `done` + comment with evidence (PR, files, verification). Status/priority/assignee/labels/description must match reality every session — update, do not leave stale.
6. Relations: `subtask` (epic parent → child), `blocks` when one task gates another, `related` otherwise.
7. Comments for decisions, blockers, UAT results. Never drop required fields.

Auth fail: `mcp_auth` on `user-kaneo`, inspect, retry once.
